OL,3,AWhat strike on Russian ship in Libya
OL,4,Asays about spread of Ukraine war
OL,5,
OL,6,FAnchored in a Mediterranean harbour
OL,7,Fnearly 2,000 miles from Moscow, the
OL,8,FCaptain of Russia's corvette Merkury
OL,9,Fmight well have thought his ship was
OL,10,Fsafe from attack. It wasn't.
OL,12,FThe audacious and successful night-time
OL,13,Fattack in Benghazi, co-ordinated by
OL,14,FUkraine's SBU intelligence agency and
OL,15,Fits armed forces, has raised the
OL,16,Fobvious question: is the Ukraine war
OL,17,Fspreading well beyond its borders?
OL,23,APub: 23-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,0,100
PN,11914
SC,0014
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F119A1795481265
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AWhat strike on Russian ship in Libya
OL,4,Asays about spread of Ukraine war
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe answer is yes, in fact, it was
OL,7,Falready spreading. But this attack,
OL,8,Fwhich Ukraine's President Volodymyr
OL,9,FZelensky called "an exemplary
OL,10,Foperation" will inevitably raise the
OL,11,Fstakes another notch.
OL,13,FRussia, which is currently engaged in a
OL,14,Fnon-stop campaign to batter Ukraine's
OL,15,Fcivilian population into submission
OL,16,Fwith daily missile and drone strikes,
OL,17,Fhas called it "a dangerous escalation".
OL,23,APub: 23-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG14/39
